f as its *pushFrame: f entered as this loop enters a pushed frame,"] [56 1 "// the eval breaker's error raised in f, and no C level counted (a Python call is none: run's check is Go's entry)."] [60 18 "// f_back of an escaped frame reaches its callers (202b)"] [68 31 "// a direct callee's RESUME error, raised in it as in a pushed frame"] [69 31 "// RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go)"] [78 41 "// sys.monitoring's PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW (queue 220; breakMonitor)"] [86 1 "// loop is runFrames's loop from its entry frame f, entered (f_back, the depth, the thread's frame) and past its RESUME:"] [87 1 "// pending, when not nil, is the error f's first step raises (queue 330: a generator's frame goes on here from its"] [88 1 "// yield-from once its delegate, resumed by resume itself, is done)."] [98 37 "// PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD (queue 220): a callback's error raised in f"] [102 5 "// a jump (f_lineno) from the yield's event: the frame goes on there, the value not yielded"] [103 5 "// (INSTRUMENTED_YIELD_VALUE's frame->instr_ptr check; queue 281: test_sys_settrace's test_jump_from_yield)"] [109 4 "// f returned v"] [117 21 "// a suspended generator's f_back is None (its caller may be reused: releaseFrame)"] [128 5 "// callInit's __init__ returned: the instance is the call's value (type_call's check of __init__'s)"] [135 4 "// the moment at a frame's return (finAtReturn): one load and a compare while no object with a __del__"] [136 4 "// made by a frame this deep is waiting"] [146 4 "// a call of a Python function from f: run the callee in this loop. The thread's reused signal lets go of the"] [147 4 "// callee once taken (py-regress-1126: it held the last frame pushed, an __init__'s with its instance, from outside"] [148 4 "// the collection's graph, so a cycle through it was never garbage: test_traceback's test_print_traceback_at_exit;"] [149 4 "// py-mp-1125, the same fix: an escaped frame's locals, sys._getframe(0)'s or a warning's f_back, outlived the"]